@startuml SAME70_XDMAC_Async_Sequence
title SAME70 XDMAC Asynchronous Multi-Channel System (Real DMA Benefits)

participant Main as main
participant Console as configure_console
participant USART_Init as DRV_USART_Comm_Init
participant UART_Init as DRV_UART_Comm_Init
participant USART_DMA as DRV_USART_DMA_Send_Recv
participant UART_DMA as DRV_UART_DMA_Send_Recv
participant XDMAC as XDMAC_Controller
participant Handler as XDMAC_Handler
participant NVIC as NVIC_Controller

note over Main : System Initialization Phase
Main -> Main : sysclk_init()
Main -> Main : board_init()
Main -> Console : configure_console()
Main -> Main : pmc_enable_periph_clk(ID_XDMAC)

note over Main : USART/UART Initialization (8 channels)
loop All 8 Channels Init
    Main -> USART_Init : DRV_USART_Comm_Init() / DRV_UART_Comm_Init()
    USART_Init -> USART_Init : Setup GPIO, Enable Peripheral, Configure
    USART_Init --> Main : 0 (success)
end

note over Main : **IDEAL DMA USAGE** - Asynchronous Multi-Channel Operation
loop while(1)
    Main -> Main : ioport_toggle_pin_level(LED_0_PIN)

    == **Concurrent DMA Setup Phase** ==
    note over Main, XDMAC : **START ALL 8 CHANNELS CONCURRENTLY** (Non-blocking)
    
    Main -> USART_DMA : **Start USART0 TX** (Non-blocking)
    activate USART_DMA
    USART_DMA -> XDMAC : Setup & Enable DMA Channel 1
    activate XDMAC
    USART_DMA --> Main : **IMMEDIATE RETURN** (DMA running in background)
    deactivate USART_DMA
    
    Main -> USART_DMA : **Start USART0 RX** (Non-blocking) 
    activate USART_DMA
    USART_DMA -> XDMAC : Setup & Enable DMA Channel 2
    USART_DMA --> Main : **IMMEDIATE RETURN** (DMA running in background)
    deactivate USART_DMA
    
    Main -> UART_DMA : **Start UART0 TX** (Non-blocking)
    activate UART_DMA
    UART_DMA -> XDMAC : Setup & Enable DMA Channel 7
    UART_DMA --> Main : **IMMEDIATE RETURN** (DMA running in background)
    deactivate UART_DMA
    
    note over Main : **ALL 8 CHANNELS STARTED IN PARALLEL**
    note over Main : **CPU FREE TO DO OTHER WORK!**
    
    == **CPU Does Other Work While DMA Transfers** ==
    Main -> Main : **Process other tasks** (calculations, GPIO, etc.)
    Main -> Main : **Handle other interrupts**
    Main -> Main : **Execute application logic**
    
    == **Background DMA Transfers** ==
    note over XDMAC : **DMA Channel 1**: USART0 TX → Memory to Peripheral
    note over XDMAC : **DMA Channel 2**: USART0 RX → Peripheral to Memory  
    note over XDMAC : **DMA Channel 7**: UART0 TX → Memory to Peripheral
    note over XDMAC : **ALL OTHER CHANNELS** running simultaneously
    
    == **Interrupt-Driven Completion** ==
    XDMAC --> Handler : **Channel 1 Complete Interrupt**
    activate Handler
    Handler -> Handler : g_xdmac_channel_done[1] = 1
    deactivate Handler
    
    XDMAC --> Handler : **Channel 2 Complete Interrupt**
    activate Handler  
    Handler -> Handler : g_xdmac_channel_done[2] = 1
    deactivate Handler
    
    XDMAC --> Handler : **Channel 7 Complete Interrupt**
    activate Handler
    Handler -> Handler : g_xdmac_channel_done[7] = 1
    deactivate Handler
    
    note over Handler : **All channels complete independently**
    
    == **Check Results (Non-blocking)** ==
    Main -> Main : **Check USART0 TX Status**
    alt DMA Complete
        Main -> Main : Process USART0 TX completion
    else Still Running
        Main -> Main : Continue other work
    end
    
    Main -> Main : **Check USART0 RX Status**  
    alt Data Received
        Main -> Main : Process received data
    else No Data Yet
        Main -> Main : Continue other work
    end
    
    deactivate XDMAC
    Main -> Main : delay_ms(1000)
end

note over Main, Handler : **KEY DMA BENEFITS SHOWN:**
note over Main, Handler : ✅ **Non-blocking**: CPU free during transfers
note over Main, Handler : ✅ **Concurrent**: 8 channels operate simultaneously  
note over Main, Handler : ✅ **Interrupt-driven**: Efficient completion notification
note over Main, Handler : ✅ **Scalable**: Easy to add more channels

== **Current Implementation Problem** ==
note over Main, USART_DMA : **CURRENT CODE ISSUE**: Blocking wait loops
note over Main, USART_DMA : ❌ while(timeout--) { if(channel_done) break; }
note over Main, USART_DMA : ❌ This defeats DMA's purpose!

== **Recommended Improvement** ==
note over Main, Handler : **BETTER APPROACH**: Event-driven or callback-based
note over Main, Handler : ✅ Start DMA → Return immediately
note over Main, Handler : ✅ Use interrupts or polling in main loop
note over Main, Handler : ✅ Process completion when ready

group XDMAC_Handler() - Interrupt Processing
    Handler -> Handler : global_status = XDMAC->XDMAC_GIS
    loop Active Channels Processing
        Handler -> Handler : channel = __builtin_ctz(global_status)
        Handler -> Handler : channel_status = XDMAC_CIS
        Handler -> Handler : if (XDMAC_CIS_BIS) set done flag
    end
end

@enduml